          "text": "no one buys their gold, silver, precious stones, and pearls; their goods of linen, purple cloth, silk, and scarlet cloth; all kinds of rare woods and all kinds of objects made of ivory and of expensive wood, of bronze, iron, and marble; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "REV.18.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "REV.18.12"
            ]
          }
        },
